  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- ${e}^{2y}{y}^{\u2033}-{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2032}+3=0$\n- ${e}^{x}{y}^{\u2033}+4{y}^{\u2032}-x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=2$\n- ${y}^{\u2033}-2x{y}^{\u2032}+5y=x$",
  "worked_solution": "\u0410 second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{\u2033}+b(x){y}^{\u2032}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{2y}{y}^{\u2033}-{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2032}+3=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${e}^{2y}{y}^{\u2033}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}{y}^{\u2033}+4{y}^{\u2032}-x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=2\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)={e}^{x},b(x)=4,c(x)=0,$ and $f(x)=2+x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}-2x{y}^{\u2032}+5y=x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=-2x,c(x)=5,$ and $f(x)=x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
